/*
Problem: Row with Max 1s (GFG)

Description:
Given a boolean matrix where each row contains only 0s and 1s,
find the index of the row having the maximum number of 1s.
Return -1 if no 1 is present in the matrix.

Approach:
- Traverse each row of the matrix.
- Count the number of 1s in that row.
- Keep track of the maximum count and its row index.
- Return the row index having the maximum number of 1s.

*/

class Solution {
public:
    int rowWithMax1s(vector<vector<int>> &mat) {
        int maxrow1 = -1;
        int n = mat.size();
        int m = mat[0].size();

        int max1 = 0;
        int count = 0;

        for(int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            for(int j = 0; j < m; j++) {
                if(mat[i][j] == 1) {
                    count++;
                }
            }

            if(count > max1) {
                max1 = count;
                maxrow1 = i;
            }

            count = 0;
        }

        return maxrow1;
    }
};

/*
Time Complexity: O(n * m)

Space Complexity: O(1)

Important Notes:
- This brute-force solution works for both sorted and unsorted matrices.
- Returns -1 if the matrix contains no 1s.
- Easy to understand and implement.

Possible Optimization:
- If each row is sorted, use Binary Search to find the first 1 in every row.
  Time Complexity: O(n log m)

- Most Optimal:
  Start from the top-right corner and move left/down.
  Time Complexity: O(n + m)

Concepts Learned:
- Matrix Traversal
- Counting Frequency
- Maintaining Maximum while Traversing

My Mistakes / Misconceptions:
- Don't assume this is the optimal solution if the matrix rows are sorted.
- Always read constraints carefully. If rows are sorted, a better approach exists.
- Handle empty matrix separately if the platform allows n = 0.
*/
